      "actor": "EHR System / Router",
      "status": "completed",
      "notes": "No protocol tasks, no trackboard indicator, no consult — and that restraint is the point. What the EHR does create is a re-screen due date, so the negative result has a shelf life. A clinician can still escalate on judgment despite it. Note also what is absent: no suicide-safer-care EpisodeOfCare opens, so this ED visit is a plain R4 Encounter rather than a SPiER one, and the episode-based measures never see it.",
